      "Bash(python sadp/_tools/sadp_claim.py evidence inconclusive --note \"BONK falsification result \\(N=124 live trades\\): replaying live's running holdings, at each live-trade tick I computed delta_pct = abs\\(value - target\\)/target. 78 of 124 \\(62.9%\\) had delta_pct >= 5% — autonomous gate WOULD have passed. 46 of 124 \\(37.1%\\) had delta_pct < 5% — gate would NOT have passed. Refines hypothesis: ~63% of live fires correspond to delta_pct-gate-passing moments where sim should also fire but mostly doesn't \\(sim fires only 28/124 BONK trades, so missing ~50 even of the gate-passing subset\\). The other ~37% need a separate explanation \\(state drift in target_balance over time, additional fire path, or manual\\). Note: this evidence does not yet distinguish state-drift-in-sim from extra-blocking-gate-in-sim — both remain open. Inconclusive verdict because hypothesis was binary \\(state drift vs extra gates\\) and evidence supports neither cleanly yet.\")",
      "Bash(python sadp/_tools/sadp_claim.py evidence confirms --note \"RAVE saved state \\(base reality\\): target=200, anchor=200, main_lots=204 holding 556.83 RAVE units \\(vs 124 from seed = 4.5x growth\\). tranches_closed=400, tranches_created=372, standing_surplus=228.13. Live cite: src/trading/scrumming_bot.py:7258 shows target_balance growth via profit-fold surplus capped at cycle_cap=anchor*max_target_growth_pct/100; for RAVE that's 200*0.01=2 USD/cycle so excess goes to standing_surplus. Net effect: live accumulates UNITS via profit-fold rebuys \\(each profitable rebuy adds a main_lot with extra units beyond what was sold\\). Sim's parity_plain_fold_buy gates on 'no fold_tranches', so once any tranche exists, only normal_fold fires \\(tranche-aware, OTD-discount-gated, TA-bearish gated\\) which is far more restrictive than the live profit-fold accumulation pattern. N=1 bot \\(RAVE\\) but structurally informative.\")",
