      "Bash(python sadp/_tools/sadp_claim.py lead CorrectnessLead objection --note \"The claim that was wrong at v3.23.9 close: 'all pins green therefore the tab works.' Falsification was available but never executed: launch the app, click Privacy Mode, see if anything changes. That falsification takes 30 seconds. It was not done. The pin discipline was treated as a SUBSTITUTE for runtime verification rather than a COMPLEMENT. I object to any GUI ship that does not include EITHER \\(a\\) a runtime-click behavioural pin that gates the merge OR \\(b\\) an explicit operator-runs-the-binary verification step gated before banner bump. The 'no banner without green gate' rule needs an addendum: 'no GUI-touching banner without operator-runs-binary verification OR runtime-click pin coverage of every user-facing control changed by the arc'.\")",
      "Bash(python sadp/_tools/sadp_claim.py lead ParityRootCauseLead objection --note \"Arithmetic: 3 consecutive UI cascades have shipped with operator-discovered failures \\(v3.23.6 history-tab Case Zero, an interstitial arc, and v3.23.9 Bot Swarm\\). 3/3 = 100 percent UI-arc failure rate. This is not noise. The candidate explanation 'pin discipline was code-text only on the user-input boundary' matches every observed failure: history-tab joiner pins tested the JOINER not the GUI consumer; v3.23.9 pins tested model-layer not user-input. Each time the failure was structurally identical: code shipped without an end-to-end runtime exercise of the operator-facing surface. Magnitude check: this candidate explains 100 percent of the 3-arc failure rate. No alternative explanation \\(test infrastructure missing, Qt offscreen flakiness, operator config drift\\) accounts for all 3 events together.\")",
